NAME
    scrape - inspect game artwork coverage, plan scrapes, and run the scraper

SYNOPSIS
    scrape ls   [<choice>...] [--kinds <kind>,...|theme] [--videos]
    scrape plan [<choice>...] [<option>...]
    scrape run  [<choice>...] [<option>...]
    scrape run  --resume
    scrape status
    scrape wait [scrape<n>]

    choices: --system <es-de name>[,...]  --favorites  --collection <name>
             --missing <kind>[,...]|any|metadata  <path>...  (or paths on
             standard input)
    options: --kinds <kind>,...|theme  --videos  --overwrite
             --region <region>  --language <language>  --threads <n>

DESCRIPTION
    Command-line interface to EmuSen's shared scraper (emusen-scrape) via
    the emusen.scrape and emusen.games services. All quota accounting,
    source ordering (ScreenScraper, then enabled OpenEmu sources), and
    media storage under /Media are shared across the process. In a
    standalone shell without a running host, the platform library opens
    the scraper from settings on first use.

    Data lines are written to standard output for piping; summaries and
    diagnostics go to standard error. Network requests to ScreenScraper
    are sent only by 'scrape run'.

    When no choice flags or paths are given, every library game not marked
    "Exclude from multi-scraper" is selected. Paths passed as arguments or
    on standard input (one per line, using the first tab-separated field
    so 'scrape ls' pipes directly into 'scrape plan' or 'scrape run')
    select named games explicitly, overriding the exclusion flag.

    With no '--kinds', runs request all nine still-image kinds a theme can
    draw: cover, screenshot, marquee, titlescreen, miximage, backcover,
    3dbox, physicalmedia, and fanart. Videos and manuals are requested
    only when explicitly asked ('--videos' is required to fetch videos
    even when 'video' appears in '--kinds' or the active theme).

    Files larger than 1 GiB are fingerprinted by size plus the SHA-1 of
    the first and last MiB (~2 MiB read) and queried by name and size
    first, falling back to full-file hashing only on a miss. Smaller files
    are hashed in full up front.

OPTIONS
    ls [<choice>...] [--kinds <kind>,...|theme] [--videos]
        Print one tab-separated line per chosen game:
        <path>  <system>  <kind>=<source> ...
        where <source> is package, hand, esde, screenscraper, openemu,
        other_game, or '-' when missing.

    plan [<choice>...] [<option>...]
        Print key<TAB>value cost and quota estimates (games,
        not_yet_asked, asked_again, complete, max_requests,
        expected_requests, expected_mb, requests_left_today, minutes,
        usable, why_not, kinds) and a one-line summary on standard error.

    run [<choice>...] [<option>...]
        Print the plan summary to standard error, then scrape chosen games
        and print one tab-separated result line per finished game:
        <outcome>  <path>  <kinds saved, or ->  [openemu]  [<detail>]
        where <outcome> is found, unknown, failed, skipped, or unchanged.
        Refuses if another scrape run is already active.

    run --resume
        Continue an interrupted scrape run with its remaining queued games
        (cannot be combined with choice flags or '--kinds').

    status
        Print current ScreenScraper quota fields (quota.*), member sign-in
        status, developer credential source (tree, user, embedded, or
        none), and active run state. Never prints credentials or passwords.

    wait [scrape<n>]
        Follow a background scrape job until completion.

    --system <name>[,...]
        Restrict selection to the listed ES-DE system names (snes, psx,
        megadrive, ...).

    --favorites, --favourites
        Restrict selection to favourite games.

    --collection <name>
        Restrict selection to members of collection <name> (case-
        insensitive).

    --missing <kind>[,...]|any|metadata
        Select games missing all listed kinds, missing any requested kind
        ('any'), or lacking a description ('metadata').

    --kinds <kind>,...|theme
        Choose media kinds from cover, screenshot, marquee, titlescreen,
        miximage, backcover, 3dbox, physicalmedia, fanart, manual, video;
        or 'theme' to query the active big-picture theme's required kinds
        (requires a running host with a loaded theme).

    --videos
        Enable video downloads.

    --overwrite
        Re-fetch media and metadata even where already present ('plan' and
        'run' only).

    --region <region>, --language <language>, --threads <n>
        Override region, language, or worker thread count (> 0, bounded by
        account limits) for 'plan' and 'run'.

JOBS AND FILES
    A run that exceeds the foreground budget continues in the background
    as scrape<n>; use ps(1) to inspect progress, 'scrape wait' to
    reattach, and kill(1) to cancel remaining queued games.

        /Media/media.db, /Media/...      Scraper database and stored media.
        /Logs/scrape_<yyyyMMdd>.log      Per-request and per-run log
                                         (no credentials are written).

EXAMPLES
    scrape ls --system snes --kinds theme
    scrape ls --kinds theme --missing any | scrape plan --kinds theme
    scrape plan --favorites --kinds cover,marquee,3dbox
    scrape run --collection Couch --videos
    scrape status | grep '^quota\.'

EXIT STATUS
    0   Command succeeded (for 'run', completed with no failures).
    1   Invalid arguments, active run conflict, missing theme service for
        '--kinds theme', or one or more scrape failures.

SEE ALSO
    rom(1), pkg(1), ps(1), kill(1), hier(7)
